## 2. SEO standards per product page

Every live product page must have:

- [ ] Rank Math focus keyphrase set in wp-admin (not auto-generated)
- [ ] Rank Math meta description = the `blurb` field (≤155 chars, ends with a CTA)
- [ ] Featured image uploaded to the WC product (1200×750 px, WebP preferred)
- [ ] At least one internal link from another page (About, Now, or a blog post)
- [ ] FAQPage JSON-LD (auto-output by `single-product.blade.php` when `faq` array is non-empty)
- [ ] SoftwareApplication + Product JSON-LD (auto-output by `single-product.blade.php`)

Target Rank Math score: **80+** per product.

---

## 3. Archive (shop) page standards

The shop listing at `/shop/` is a WooCommerce archive routed through `archive-product.blade.php`. Its editable copy is on the WooCommerce "Shop" page in wp-admin via **Page content (theme)** fields.

Required schema on the shop page:
- `CollectionPage` with `hasPart` array of product URLs (auto-output)
- `FAQPage` when FAQ items are set (auto-output)

Required SEO defaults:
- Title: "WordPress Themes, Plugins & Web Apps | Matt Hummel"
- Meta description: covers themes + plugins + apps, ends with CTA (set in `app/filters.php → mh_seo_meta_description()`)

---

## 4. Single product page layout order

Do not reorder these sections without a strong reason:

1. Hero — product title, price, buy/demo CTAs, trust signals
2. Summary — full overview paragraph (context before screenshots)
3. Screenshots gallery
4. Features / benefits (What you get)
5. Story — challenge + approach (Built for this niche / The approach)
6. Deliverables (What's included)
7. Hire nudge strip (Need it customized?)
8. Gutenberg blocks (themes only)
9. Technical / Stack & code
10. Documentation links
11. FAQ (accordion, drives FAQPage schema)
12. Purchase CTA band

---

## 5. `mh_product_entry()` — adding a new field

When you need a field not in the JSON catalog, follow this pattern in `app/shop.php`:

1. Add the key to the JSON catalog under the product.
2. In `mh_product_entry()`, read it from `$entry` (already merged from JSON + meta).
3. In the Blade template, extract it from `$entry` at the top `@php` block.
4. Do NOT hardcode copy in the template.

Do not install ACF or add a new metabox for product fields — use `_mh_project_*` meta (saved by the catalog seed) or `mh_product_entry()`.

---

## 6. Pricing rules

- Free product: `price` = 0 or empty, `is_free: true` in catalog JSON.
- Paid product: one-time price in USD, no subscription or recurring unless Matt explicitly requests.
- Do not create coupon logic, upsell popups, or "limited time" countdowns without Matt's approval.
- WooCommerce checkout is the only purchase flow. Do not add Stripe or Paddle SDKs directly.

---

## 7. SEO title format

Built in `app/filters.php → mh_seo_document_title()`:

- Shop archive: `WordPress Themes, Plugins & Web Apps | [Brand]`
- Product (theme): `[Product name] | WordPress Theme | [Brand]`
- Product (plugin): `[Product name] | WordPress Plugin | [Brand]`
- Product (app): `[Product name] | Web App | [Brand]`
- All clipped at 60 characters.

Do not override these with a custom filter unless the product has a Rank Math title explicitly set in wp-admin (that wins automatically).
